WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.444 --> 00:00:03.260
- [Narrator] Music plays an
important role in our lives.

00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.442
It can help is relax, concentrate,

00:00:05.442 --> 00:00:07.381
or get pumped for a work out.

00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:09.082
And if this song makes you happy,

00:00:09.082 --> 00:00:12.165
well, it's because it's
affecting your brain chemistry.

00:00:12.165 --> 00:00:15.479
So why do we find music so enjoyable?

00:00:15.479 --> 00:00:18.592
Researchers from McGill
University in Montreal

00:00:18.592 --> 00:00:21.182
found that dopamine
releases during moments

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:23.196
of enjoyment while listening to music.

00:00:23.196 --> 00:00:24.983
It's what gives us the chills.

00:00:24.983 --> 00:00:29.140
The same chemical reaction
as when you fall in love.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.019
Basically, listening to music is amazing

00:00:32.019 --> 00:00:34.579
and your brain loves it.

00:00:34.579 --> 00:00:37.203
Music also distracts your
brain from registering

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.618
the body's fatigue.

00:00:38.618 --> 00:00:40.928
It increases endurance while improving

00:00:40.928 --> 00:00:42.230
the heart and muscles,

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:45.379
giving music both a
psychological and physiological

00:00:45.379 --> 00:00:47.129
impact on the body.

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:48.927
Think about that next
time you're at the gym

00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:51.177
and forget your headphones.

00:00:52.091 --> 00:00:54.275
And did you know that
playing a musical instrument

00:00:54.275 --> 00:00:55.689
can make you smarter?

00:00:55.689 --> 00:00:58.112
And more of an annoying neighbor.

00:00:58.112 --> 00:00:59.714
Sorry Charlie.

00:00:59.714 --> 00:01:02.188
Believe it or not, children
with at least three

00:01:02.188 --> 00:01:04.555
years of musical training performed better

00:01:04.555 --> 00:01:06.988
during testing for nonverbal reasoning,

00:01:06.988 --> 00:01:10.323
fine motor skills,
auditory discrimination,

00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:13.152
and vocabulary than those who did not.

00:01:13.152 --> 00:01:16.043
We generally don't
realize how a simple song

00:01:16.043 --> 00:01:17.831
can affect our brains and bodies.

00:01:17.831 --> 00:01:20.494
Nevertheless, music has
a measurably significant

00:01:20.494 --> 00:01:23.712
effect on human beings,
influencing the way we dance,

00:01:23.712 --> 00:01:26.056
exercise, and think.

00:01:26.056 --> 00:01:28.789
So how has music affected your life?

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:31.372
(upbeat music)

